{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they hammered out the plates of gold.</b> The Ramban wrote: Scripture did not add, in all the work of the sanctuary, to explain the manner of the craft how it was made, except here. And it would have been fitting to say, 'And they made the ephod of gold, blue, and purple,' for so is the way in all of them." "<b>And it is fitting</b> that it recounted here the device they innovated for the threads of gold, for it was a wonder in their eyes that gold should be spun and plyed as is done with wool and linen, for it had never been heard until that day to do so. End of his words."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:50.883223650Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}